From 699ce5000c5559dbc5ae6c2cf1a42db1fc0a253b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:46:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 369/369] review fixes: couple probe to export (no frozen
 feed), surface probe auto-enable, drop dead mp4 slop

Follow-ups from the v2.3.0 pre-distribution review (docs/BACKLOG.md):
- [Med] Probe/export decouple. reaper_export.cgi action=probe now REFUSES to turn the
  health probe off while reaper_export_mode != off - it would freeze health.json while
  rexport keeps POSTing the stale snapshot. Turning ON is always allowed; set the mode
  to Off to stop collecting. Reaper_Analytics.asp guards the toggle proactively (shows
  RANL_50) and handles the export_armed rejection.
- [Low] Probe auto-enable was invisible on Reaper_Storage.asp: the export-mode note now
  states that any non-off mode enables the probe (RDST_63).
- [Low] Removed the dead **.mp4 handler in httpd/basic.c (basic.o is not linked into
  httpd; the live table is web.c's, already clean) - slop from the mp4->APNG saga.
- Dicts: RANL_50 + RDST_63, lockstep 6076 x25.

Reviewed, not changed (documented tradeoffs): rtrafd DHCP-churn mis-merge (a freshness
gate would defeat the dedup, which by design targets stale/offline slots) and phantom-
history discard (~0 bytes on offline flows; folding rings risks the hot path for no gain).
"Off persists nothing" is already release-noted in the v2.3.0 CHANGELOG. rexport.sh nvram
values are curl-config-quoted (post-auth admin only; no shell injection).

v2.3.0.
